  "term": "sensory field",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, a sensory field is a sensory area represented on the cerebral cortex, with parts corresponding to regions of the body or to a particular sense. Its exact borders are described as hard to fix because these cortical representations overlap and work together as part of a larger whole.",
